            <div xml:id="d530">

                <pb facs="0693" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5844a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-21T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>66. Legation Managua telegraphs<anchor n="17" xml:id="d530-f1"/> reliable
                    information indicates that what is apparently main body Sandino’s force is just
                    north of Patuca River in disputed boundary area in very favorable position for
                    aerial attack. General Feland, General McCoy and Eberhardt consider matter so
                    important that they are sending Munro to Tegucigalpa by aeroplane today to
                    discuss matter with you. Please take matter up immediately upon Munro’s arrival
                    with President Paz and endeavor to obtain an immediate consent to this action
                    and cable authority to Managua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
